  "security_implications": "The transmit data path uses parity for integrity, but err_o from the transmit FIFO is unconnected; any FIFO internal error (overrun, underrun) is silently ignored, potentially leading to corrupted data transmission without detection. The loopback mode bypasses all transmit framing and parity, directly forwarding rx to tx, which could expose raw receive data without integrity checks. No access controls on loopback or parity settings are visible in this chunk.",
  "evidence_refs": [
